itLab, keep it open in Plane and move it to the next sprint\\n- If the issue is closed in GitLab, close it in Plane\\n\\nSince the second issue doesn\\'t exist in GitLab at all, I closed it in Plane.\\n', action=<ActionType.THINK: 'think'>), AgentThinkObservation(content='Your thought has been logged.', observation=<ObservationType.THINK: 'think'>), MCPAction(name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'Plane', 'operation': 'SyncIssuesWithGitLab', 'details': '\\n# Sync Issues Between Plane and GitLab\\n\\n## Purpose\\nSynchronize issue status between Plane and GitLab based on the following rules:\\n- If an issue is open in GitLab, keep it open in Plane and move it to the next sprint\\n- If an issue is closed in GitLab, close it in Plane\\n\\n## Steps\\n\\n### 1. Check GitLab Status\\n- Navigate to GitLab issues page: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/janusgraph/-/issues/?state=all\\n- Use the search function to find specific issues by title\\n- Note the status (Open/Closed) for each issue\\n\\n### 2. Update Plane Issues\\n- Navigate to Plane issues page: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/f04e5c07-8fa2-4eaf-a35b-5cacf3f1d025/issues/\\n- For issues that are OPEN in GitLab:\\n  - Click the Sprint dropdown (button with sprint name)\\n  - Select the next sprint (e.g., \"Sprint 2\")\\n- For issues that are CLOSED in GitLab (or not found):\\n  - Click the Status dropdown (button with current status)\\n  - Select \"Cancelled\" to close the issue\\n\\n### 3. Verification\\n- Confirm that issues have been moved to the correct sprint\\n- Confirm that closed issues show \"Cancelled\" status\\n- Verify the total issue count remains consistent\\n\\n## Notes\\n- This process ensures alignment between development tracking (Plane) and source control (GitLab)\\n- Issues not found in GitLab should be considered closed/cancelled\\n- Always verify both systems before and after synchronization\\n'}, thought='Now let me save this experience to the SOP guide for future reference.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Successfully saved new guide \\'SyncIssuesWithGitLab\\' for platform \\'Plane\\'.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'Plane', 'operation': 'SyncIssuesWithGitLab', 'details': '\\n# Sync Issues Between Plane and GitLab\\n\\n## Purpose\\nSynchronize issue status between Plane and GitLab based on the following rules:\\n- If an issue is open in GitLab, keep it open in Plane and move it to the next sprint\\n- If an issue is closed in GitLab, close it in Plane\\n\\n## Steps\\n\\n### 1. Check GitLab Status\\n- Navigate to GitLab issues page: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/janusgraph/-/issues/?state=all\\n- Use the search function to find specific issues by title\\n- Note the status (Open/Closed) for each issue\\n\\n### 2. Update Plane Issues\\n- Navigate to Plane issues page: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/f04e5c07-8fa2-4eaf-a35b-5cacf3f1d025/issues/\\n- For issues that are OPEN in GitLab:\\n  - Click the Sprint dropdown (button with sprint name)\\n  - Select the next sprint (e.g., \"Sprint 2\")\\n- For issues that are CLOSED in GitLab (or not found):\\n  - Click the Status dropdown (button with current status)\\n  - Select \"Cancelled\" to close the issue\\n\\n### 3. Verification\\n- Confirm that issues have been moved to the correct sprint\\n- Confirm that closed issues show \"Cancelled\" status\\n- Verify the total issue count remains consistent\\n\\n## Notes\\n- This process ensures alignment between development tracking (Plane) and source control (GitLab)\\n- Issues not found in GitLab should be considered closed/cancelled\\n- Always verify both systems before and after synchronization\\n'}), AgentFinishAction(final_thought='Task completed successfully! I have synchro